<title>FRANCE: Strafor sells Bongard unit.</title>
<headline>Strafor sells Bongard unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French industrial equipment supplier Strafor Facom said on Monday that it had sold all but a 19 percent stake in its bakery equipment subsidiary Bongard.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it had sold 75 percent of Bongard to Schroder Ventures, six percent to Bongard managers and would retain 19 percent.</p>
<p>Strafor Facom did not disclose terms but said Bongard employs 550 people and generated 432 million francs in sales in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
